# Response headers for the Cloudflare Worker's static assets. wrangler parses
# this file out of the assets directory and the asset router applies the rules.
#
# It exists because of what the move off Pages took away. Cloudflare Pages added
# the two headers below to every response it served, automatically, with nothing
# in this repository asking for them — this file did not exist and never has.
# Workers Static Assets does not, so without this rule homiio.com would have
# lost both at cutover, silently, since no build, deploy or test here reads a
# response header.
#
# Measured on a Pages hostname whose project has no `_headers` rule for them
# either, which is what shows they come from the platform rather than any
# project:
#
#   oxy-auth.pages.dev  referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
#                       x-content-type-options: nosniff
#
# `nosniff` is the one that matters: without it a browser may disregard a
# declared Content-Type and sniff the bytes instead, which turns any response
# carrying attacker-influenced content into a possible script.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
